+## Why `public/` exists
+
+`wrangler.jsonc` points Workers Static Assets only at `./public`. Dependencies, tests, `functions/`, Worker source, and `node_modules/` are therefore never uploaded as website assets. This avoids the prior `workerd` >25 MiB static-asset deployment failure.
+
+`public/_headers` is supported by Workers Static Assets and applies the existing security/cache headers to static responses. `/download` is generated by Worker code, so `src/index.js` adds the security headers directly to its redirect response.
+
